y conservative circle includes  um  race-based jokes that i find completely  gross  and it all it also includes certain  ideology when it comes to government  regulation and covid and the like i mean  the guy has said  he has seen  the wacky texas governor greg abbott  personally since he has moved to texas  abbott's completely out of his mind and  rogan from what i've heard acts like  greg abbott is a reasonable normal  person to be listening to listening to  so there's both  the audience of rogan skews culturally  conservative  um and in addition to that he's in these  culturally conservative circles which  makes it so that he has more right-wing  guests than left-wing guests now there's  a list that has been spreading of  rogan's right wing guests versus left  wing and the right wing list is much  longer the right wing list is much  longer at the same time there were some  notable people missing from the left  wing guests that he has had on me for  example i wasn't on that list i've been  on twice so i think with all of these no  one thing really tells us everything  about this story but the real concern i  have is he's already  in a sort of right-wing echo chamber  because he has gone to texas and he's  hanging out with greg abbott and all  these other people uh because he is  getting the most positive feedback from  the right wing who says his racial  comments are perfectly fine his coveted  comments are perfectly fine and so the  concern is it's only gonna get worse  and i think it's unlikely  that um  spotify is going to drop him at this  point in time and from a very practical  perspective one of the worst things i  can imagine  is the show just getting more right wing  that that seems like it would be a bad  thing so uh that's my general  perspective on this at this point in  time  uh the things that that rogan has said  are completely indefensible and he  doesn't seem to be defending them and  there's questions as to whether the  apology is sincere or not 